        "title": "Impressive temple",
        "text": "One of 12 jyotirlingas, this 15th cent. Temple is a UNESCO World heritage site. Photography is not permitted within the temple premises.\nThere are many temples and shrines in the inner courtyard and outer complex.\nThe main temple has Nepalese pagoda style of architecture with cubic constructions and carved wooden rafters on which they rest (tundal).  The two level roofs are of copper with gold covering. It has four main doors covered with silver sheets, a gold pinnacle (Gajur) and two Garbhagrihas. The Mukhalinga is 1 meter tall, has faces in four directions and a silver yoni base bound with a silver serpent.  The faces represent various aspects of Shiva - Sadyojata (aka Barun), Vamdeva (aka Ardhanareshwor), Tatpurusha, Aghor & Ishana.\nEntry is permitted from West entrance to Hindus only.  The other 3 entrances are opened during aarti only.  Rituals and viewing from 5am – 12pm and from 5pm – 7pm.  Abhishek is performed from 9am – 11am.  Buy ticket at SBI counter for NPR 1000 for Rudraabhishek.  Abhishek is done based on the direction the mukh is viewed.  If your receipt says as eastern direction then one needs to stand in the queue at the eastern entrance, wherein the priests will do the abhishek for the eastern mukh of the shivling.",
