        "title": "Fascinating at sunset",
        "text": "We went at sunset which was a perfect time to go as it seems as the sun starts to set over Kathmandu giving a glorious view. We went with the mindset of not getting a guide, but after we go a little lost we decided to pay a small fee to a gentleman with very good english who had started speaking to us upon entry. I have to admit that this was absolutely the best thing we could have done with our money, the man took us around the entire complex, taking his time to tell us all about the intricacies of the Hindu religion and the cremations. We both learnt a huge amount about the temple, and Nepalese culture in general and it was only a small fee in the grand scheme of things. If only I had his name to tell you...",
