        "title": "Impressive",
        "text": "The Pashupatinath Temple itself is not open to non-Hindu people, you can only look at the outside of the entrance, but the most impressive things happen at the riverside where the crematory ceremonies are held. Off course it feels very strange to watch people mourne and grieve about their lost loved ones, but for them it is part of daily life. They are not offended if you stay there to watch, as long as you behave in a respectfull way... it is truly impressive and something we will remember for the rest of our days.",
