      {
        "review_id": 438679643,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r438679643-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "It's definitely different and must visit ",
        "text": "I am not a religious person but I make it a point to visit key religious places in any city and it was given that I would go to see Pashupatinath temple in Kathmandu. \nIn a distant corner of city is this famous temple of lord shiva. It is world famous and one of the key tourist attraction in city. People in India recognises Kathmandu with this temple.  \nIt is spread in large area and is very serene.  The temple inside are very serene and you get feeling of calmness as soon as you enter in the premises. I was pleasantly surprised by the cleanliness and the way people organise themselves and how the things are organised. \nThe priests are very friendly and do not force you to donate or they do not Miss guide you. They are indifferent whether you donate money or not. This is not true about temples in other parts of the world where the worst experience is getting rid from greedy chase of some false preistman. In NHPS opinion this is the high point of this temple.  \nOn down side, I was disappointed that even in today's time it reads that only Hindu are allowed to enter in premises. I am sure Lord Shiva would not have differentiated by religion of the person. It is high time this age old tradition is done away with. \n\nThe complementary part of this visit is a river side behind the temple and you can see age hold Hindu traditions including cremation of dead bodies.  \n\nA must visit for all and hope that non hindu will also be allowed to enter in the Pashpatunath temple premises, hopefully very soon. ",
