        "title": "A must see...",
        "text": "A little difficult to navigate around but worth the effort. What a jaw dropping experience.  Unfortunately the temple is only open to Hindus so we couldn't access this part but the rest is without doubt the most surreal experience.\n\nDaily there are open air cremations, like statues, we stood and watched the deceased being washed, swathe in flowers and cremated.\n\nThere are signs of earthquake damage however there is still enough to see and fill half a day.\n\nLots of friendly people that turn out to be guides that would like payment. We had a guide that proved very knowledgeable and gave us the background to the proceedings.\n\nLots of monkeys!\n\n",
