      {
        "review_id": 438102223,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r438102223-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Fascinating sight to visit",
        "text": "This is a large temple complex and has extensive grounds inside so be prepared for some walking.  We went in the morning and there was  huge amount of activities going on.  By the river is where families come to conduct cremation, funereal or mourning rituals and these are fascinating to watch.  Tiull also see a lot of temple monkeys biding their time for the offerings which keeps them very well fed.  As well as real or fake shamans dressed up to get money for getting their pictures taken and persistent jewelry vendors following you around. Plan for at least two hours.  This temple is almost within walking distance from Dwarikas hotel but taxis are easy to get.",
